From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): skip empty moe_swiglu_cast slabs and cascade
 1-row PDL preloads

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 2756478b60b90700b9918b457aeb38657da637b5.

Rationale:
In vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/moe.py, moe_swiglu_cast unconditionally preloaded all rows_per_cta Order and Weights entries before pdl.chain(), and after pdl.chain() stepped through every row r in 0..rows_per_cta-1 inside an unrolled loop even when orders[0] < 0 (an empty slab, which represents 75% of active-tile CTAs in decode since active experts average 1.0-2.1 rows out of 16) or orders[1] < 0 (a 1-row tile, which represents 68%-100% of slab == 0 CTAs in decode).
Preserve rows_per_cta = 4 if warps >= 4 else 2 (keeping TP3 at rows_per_cta = 2 as measured in experiments/2026-10-18-r6w-swiglu), cascade Order and Weights preloads before pdl.chain() so empty slabs only read orders[0] and 1-row tiles only read orders[0..1] and weights[0], exit empty slabs immediately after pdl.chain() via if expert >= 0 and orders[0] >= 0:, and guard rows 1..rows_per_cta-1 behind if rows_per_cta > 1 and orders[1] >= 0:.

Quality:
Bit-identical (torch.equal, 0 uint16 diffs, max_abs_diff == 0.0) across all TP4 and TP3 shapes (M = 1..48), both standalone and end-to-end inside captured decode CUDA graphs.
